      <article class="pp-content montserrat-regular">
        <section id="introduction">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">1. Introduction</h2>
          <p>
            Uncore Digital ("Uncore Digital", "we", "us" or "our") respects your
            privacy. This Privacy Policy explains what personal information we
            collect when you visit uncoredigital.com (the "Website") or contact
            us, how we use and protect it, and the choices and rights you have.
          </p>
          <p>
            By using the Website, you acknowledge that you have read this
            policy. If you do not agree with it, please do not use the Website
            or submit your information through it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="who-we-are">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">2. Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            Uncore Digital is a digital agency offering digital marketing,
            product development, digital transformation, and web and app
            development services. For the purposes of applicable data protection
            laws, Uncore Digital is the controller (in India, the "data
            fiduciary") of the personal information collected through the
            Website.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Email:</strong>
              <a href="mailto:connect@uncoredigital.com"
                >connect@uncoredigital.com</a
              >
            </li>
            <li><strong>Phone:</strong> +91 97255 18964</li>
            <li>
              <strong>Offices:</strong> 626 RXR Plaza, Uniondale, NY 11556, USA,
              and 1013, Ratnanjali, Solitaire, India
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="information-we-collect">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">3. Information we collect</h2>

          <h3 class="poppins-bold">3.1 Information you give us</h3>
          <p>
            When you fill in a contact or consultation form, request a call, or
            email us, you may provide:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Your name</li>
            <li>Your email address</li>
            <li>Your phone number</li>
            <li>The subject and content of your message</li>
            <li>
              Any other details you choose to share about your business or
              project
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Please do not send sensitive information (such as payment card
            numbers, government ID numbers or health information) through our
            forms or chat.
          </p>

          <h3 class="poppins-bold">3.2 Information collected automatically</h3>
          <p>
            When you browse the Website, we and our service providers may
            automatically collect technical and usage information, such as:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Device and browser type, operating system and screen size</li>
            <li>IP address and approximate location (country or city level)</li>
            <li>Pages visited, links clicked, time spent and referring page</li>
            <li>Date and time of your visit</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="poppins-bold">3.3 Chat conversations</h3>
          <p>
            If you use the chat assistant on the Website, we process the
            messages you send and the responses given, along with technical data
            needed to run the chat. The chat is provided by a third-party
            service provider acting on our behalf.
          </p>

          <h3 class="poppins-bold">3.4 Information from other sources</h3>
          <p>
            If you contact us through a social platform such as LinkedIn or
            Instagram, we may receive the information you share with us there,
            subject to that platform's own privacy policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="how-we-use">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">4. How we use your information</h2>
          <p>We use personal information to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Respond to your enquiries, consultation requests and messages
            </li>
            <li>
              Prepare proposals and provide and manage our services if you
              become a client
            </li>
            <li>
              Operate, maintain, secure and improve the Website and its
              performance
            </li>
            <li>
              Understand how visitors use the Website so we can improve content
              and user experience
            </li>
            <li>
              Send updates, insights or offers where you have asked for them or
              where the law allows, with an option to unsubscribe at any time
            </li>
            <li>
              Detect, prevent and respond to fraud, spam, abuse and security
              incidents
            </li>
            <li>Comply with legal obligations and enforce our rights</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it to
            make decisions that have legal or similarly significant effects on
            you through solely automated means.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="legal-bases">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">5. Legal bases for processing</h2>
          <p>
            Where laws such as the EU/UK GDPR apply, we rely on the following
            legal bases:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Consent</strong> – for example, when you submit a form
              asking us to contact you, or agree to optional cookies.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Contract</strong> – when processing is needed to provide
              services you requested or to take steps before entering into a
              contract.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Legitimate interests</strong> – such as keeping the
              Website secure, understanding how it is used and improving our
              services, where these interests are not overridden by your rights.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Legal obligation</strong> – when we must process data to
              comply with the law.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, we process
            personal data with your consent or for other legitimate uses
            permitted by the Act.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="cookies">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">6. Cookies and analytics</h2>
          <p>
            Cookies are small files stored on your device. We and our service
            providers may use cookies and similar technologies to keep the
            Website working, remember preferences, and measure usage.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Essential:</strong> needed for the Website and chat to
              function properly.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Analytics:</strong> help us understand traffic and
              performance. We use Vercel Analytics, which is designed to measure
              visits without tracking individuals across websites.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Functional:</strong> remember choices you make, such as
              chat session state.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            You can control or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking
            some cookies may affect how parts of the Website work. Our Website
            does not currently respond to "Do Not Track" browser signals, but
            you can use the browser controls above.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="sharing">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">7. Sharing your information</h2>
          <p>
            We share personal information only as described below, and we
            require our providers to protect it and use it only for the services
            they perform for us.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Service providers:</strong> companies that help us run the
              Website and our business, including website hosting and analytics
              (Vercel), email and workspace tools used to receive and process
              form submissions (Google), and chat assistant providers.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Professional advisers:</strong> lawyers, accountants and
              insurers, where needed.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Legal and safety:</strong> authorities, courts or other
              parties where we are required by law, or where needed to protect
              our rights, users or others.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Business transfers:</strong> a successor entity if we are
              involved in a merger, acquisition or sale of assets, subject to
              this policy.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We do not sell or rent your personal information to third parties.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="transfers">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">8. International transfers</h2>
          <p>
            We operate in India and the United States, and our service providers
            may process data in these and other countries. Your information may
            therefore be transferred to, and stored in, countries other than
            your own, which may have different data protection rules. Where
            required, we use appropriate safeguards, such as standard
            contractual clauses or equivalent mechanisms, to protect your
            information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="retention">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">9. Data retention</h2>
          <p>
            We keep personal information only as long as needed for the purposes
            in this policy, including to meet legal, accounting or reporting
            requirements. As a general guide:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Enquiries that do not lead to a project are kept for up to 24
              months, then deleted or anonymised.
            </li>
            <li>
              Client records are kept for the length of the engagement and the
              period required by law afterwards.
            </li>
            <li>Analytics data is kept in aggregated or anonymised form.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            You can ask us to delete your information earlier (see "Your
            rights").
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="security">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">10. Security</h2>
          <p>
            We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect
            personal information, including encrypted (HTTPS) connections,
            access controls and the use of reputable providers. No method of
            transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee
            absolute security. If a data breach affects your personal
            information, we will notify you and the relevant authorities as
            required by law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="your-rights">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">11. Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Depending on where you live, you may have some or all of the
            following rights:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Access the personal information we hold about you</li>
            <li>Correct inaccurate or incomplete information</li>
            <li>Delete your personal information</li>
            <li>Restrict or object to certain processing</li>
            <li>Receive a copy of your data in a portable format</li>
            <li>
              Withdraw consent at any time, without affecting processing that
              took place before withdrawal
            </li>
            <li>Opt out of marketing messages</li>
            <li>
              Nominate another person to exercise your rights in the event of
              death or incapacity (India)
            </li>
            <li>
              Complain to your local data protection authority, such as the Data
              Protection Board of India, an EU/UK supervisory authority, or your
              state attorney general in the US
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="poppins-bold">
            Residents of California and other US states
          </h3>
          <p>
            You may have the right to know, access, correct and delete the
            personal information we hold, and to opt out of its sale or sharing.
            We do not sell personal information or share it for cross-context
            behavioural advertising, and we will not discriminate against you
            for exercising your rights.
          </p>

          <h3 class="poppins-bold">How to exercise your rights</h3>
          <p>
            Email us at
            <a href="mailto:connect@uncoredigital.com"
              >connect@uncoredigital.com</a
            >
            with the subject line "Privacy Request". We may need to verify your
            identity before acting on a request, and we will respond within the
            time required by applicable law, generally within 30 days.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Grievance Officer (India):</strong> for complaints about how
            we handle your personal data, write to the Grievance Officer, Uncore
            Digital, at
            <a href="mailto:connect@uncoredigital.com"
              >connect@uncoredigital.com</a
            >. We aim to acknowledge complaints promptly and resolve them within
            the period required by law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="children">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">12. Children's privacy</h2>
          <p>
            The Website is intended for businesses and adults. It is not
            directed to children under 18, and we do not knowingly collect
            personal information from them. If you believe a child has given us
            personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="third-party">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">13. Third-party links</h2>
          <p>
            The Website links to other sites and platforms, including LinkedIn,
            Instagram and Pinterest. We do not control these sites and are not
            responsible for their content or privacy practices. We encourage you
            to read the privacy policy of every site you visit.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="changes">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">14. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes to
            our practices, technology or legal requirements. The "Last updated"
            date at the top shows when it was last revised. If we make material
            changes, we will take reasonable steps to let you know, for example
            by a notice on the Website.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="contact">
          <h2 class="poppins-bold">15. Contact us</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions about this policy or how we handle your
            information, please contact us:
          </p>
          <div class="pp-contact">
            <p><strong>Uncore Digital</strong></p>
            <p>
              Email:
              <a href="mailto:connect@uncoredigital.com"
                >connect@uncoredigital.com</a
              >
            </p>
            <p>Phone: +91 97255 18964</p>
            <p>626 RXR Plaza, Uniondale, NY 11556, USA</p>
            <p>1013, Ratnanjali, Solitaire, India</p>
          </div>
        </section>
